me truly great Abyssal/Deathlord victim tableaus. Some great visuals, plus a blueprint for an Abyssal villain who doesn't confront the heroes directly, preferring to remain in the shadows and send messages through his crimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T07:44:41-07:00","id":94251,"title":"","content":"I always need to watch some Fatal Frame video whenever I want to be remind that ghosts are supposed to be scary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VXYtxRxaPvw\" data-code=\"VXYtxRxaPvw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VXYtxRxaPvw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T08:07:18-07:00","id":94261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=94246#post94246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're not watching Hannibal you're (a) missing out on the best horror series on TV...</div> </div> </div> </div>I am okay with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T08:30:13-07:00","id":94270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=91699#post91699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Man with the Iron Fists</i>.<br /> <br /> Players, amirite?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say, the earlier suggestion of <i>Samurai Champloo</i> ep13 is actually a great one. I highly recommend it for piratey things.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T08:47:13-07:00","id":94273,"title":"","content":"Random list of anime I like draw on a lot for Exalted:<br /> <br /> <i>Samurai Champloo</i> - I love the fights, the way that you get a bit of the &quot;lived in, spread out and urbanized&quot; feel of Edo Japan very nicely. It also has all sorts of plot bits that are great for Exalted: magistrates, assassins, random dudes you pissed off, stumbling into conterfeit crime rings, battles, saving people, failing to save people. It might not be quite the power level Exalted gets to, but its aesthetic, plot elements, and soudntrack all are great bits to draw on for the game.<br /> <br /> <i>Magi: The Labrynth of Magic</i> - Already brought-up earlier, but wanting to reharp this one. It's a high fantasy anime that manages to not be another pseudo-Medeival DragonQuest clone, or samurai fantasy. They instead draw on the Middle East pretty heavily, and instead of &quot;centering&quot; their fantasy world on Europe, they center it in Arabia. You get characters who draw on aesthetics of the Muslim world, Persia, India, Greece, Rome, and more Germanic Europe. The world seems to run on realpolitik but at the same time has Artifacts, individuals with power influence nations, and such, but in a scale that I think 3e is going for. Dungeon Conquerers are individually powerful, but still can't get around politics. Magi have a lot of Sidereal things to draw on, including the &quot;Exalted at conception&quot; and fixed numbers. Great Exalted stuff.<br /> <br /> <i>Fate/Zero</i> - White the Fate series as a whole has some cool stuff, I think this series managed to caputre a bit of what Exalted wants to be more than the rest does. It's moslty because it does some of the showing the ambiguity of moral actions done through amoral means, the general kind of &quot;grit&quot; to the character's actions and so on. It also has great animation, fights, and character/prop designs. I think otherwise <i>Fate/prototype</i> is the way to go for a few more things, but I think these two make the best parts of design and elements to draw on for Exalted. I would say it's probably, along with <i>Magi</i>, the two shows that in my mind &quot;update&quot; Exalted sources to me.<br /> <br /> <i>Sword of the Stranger</i> - Animated movie by the same guys who did Bebop, RahXephon and a few other good ones. Samurai movie with lots of good fights, variety of characters, politics and even a bit of Taoist mysticism in there to play with. <br /> <br /> <i>From the New World</i> - Kind of more psychics and such, but I think a good demonstration of how a society can go odd in a post-apocalyptic world. Great aesthetic for Exalted in general I think, and there's a couple scenes which invoke images of the Wyld, Solar tyranny, or just plain strange critters out in the world worth looking into. Hard to talk about it much wihtout spoiling it too since it's also (IMHO) a great thriller series.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:54:11-07:00","id":94311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=89271#post89271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Exalted Media I recently discovered is Mushi-shi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mushishi has long been my &quot;go-to&quot; series any time I want to introduce something weird or unusual into Exalted. These things usually don't take center stage, but I often find that they help to flesh out the world a little bit. <br /> <br /> There's a new season of it starting up this spring by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:56:22-07:00","id":94312,"title":"","content":"For some reason, one thing that really amuses me with Magi is that the dungeon capturers have the powers of Exigents and the narrative role of Solars, while the magi have the powers of Twilights (or Daybreak for one of them) and the narrative role of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of weird that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T11:24:28-07:00","id":94349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=94312#post94312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, one thing that really amuses me with Magi is that the dungeon capturers have the powers of Exigents and the narrative role of Solars, while the magi have the powers of Twilights (or Daybreak for one of them) and the narrative role of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of weird that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a true case on that. It's not a perfect fit, but it does have a lot of good stuff to draw upon for Exalted games. <br /> <br /> I randomly like how the author seems to of set an upper bar on power level in the setting (Sinbad) and is kind of trying to, as I have seen, not break that ceiling too badly. Which is a pretty different take from a lot of shounen shows in that they usually just kind of &quot;work it out as they go along&quot; and there' smassive power inflation pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:42:20-07:00","id":94509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=92888#post92888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then clearly you need to watch more Donnie Yen. As far as current stuff goes, Wu Xia just game out last year I believe and is absolutely fantastic (Night Caste, anyone?). Though it was released stateside with the stupid and pointless title &quot;Dragon.&quot; It is available on Netflix last I checked, and I can't recommend it enough. Also, Takeshi Kaneshiro is (Of Onimusha: Warlords, The Returners, and House of Lying Daggers game) is an amazing Water aspect detective.<br /> <br /> For a pretty drastic change in style, Special ID was a really enjoyable take on the &quot;undercover cop trying to stay sane&quot; shtick (kind of like a more martial arts Departed/Infernal Affairs)<br /> <br /> A way more serious Donnie Yen is The Lost Bladesman. A biopic of a historical figure that is an Exalted if I've ever heard of one, the great general Guan Yu.<br /> <br /> Those are some of his more recent ones. Other fantastic Donnie Yen films include Killzone (AKA S.P.L), Iron Monkey, 14 Blades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently saw Wu Xia and liked everything about it, except the ending which I thought was just confusing. The fight scenes where cool though, and the acupuncture/chi energi style of medicine and martial arts felt kind of exalted, or at least a good inspiration for exalted.<br /> <br /> Iron Monkey and 14 Blades are also excellent films (actually saw 14 Blades just a few days ago, as the first film in my new quest of watching more Donnie Yen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If I ever play a lunar I'm gonna steal that moonsilver whip/spear weapon and develop my own martial art around it.)<br /> <br /> I will have to pick The Lost Bladesman up, looks very interesting. Thanks for the tip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2355-ratatosk","name":"Ratatosk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:48:02-07:00","id":94511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> 