sage\"><br /> This is a Korean movie (\ud574\uc801 : \ubc14\ub2e4\ub85c \uac04 \uc0b0\uc801) about Joseon-era pirates fighting for the dragon seal (only the emperor is allowed to use) in case anyone is interested .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am, and hope to see both of those films eventually! <br /> <br /> Jen, do you recognize the clips I put in Posts #248 &amp; #267? Have you seen those before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:30:58-08:00","id":418388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=418355#post418355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am, and hope to see both of those films eventually!<br /> <br /> Jen, do you recognize the clips I put in Posts #248 &amp; #267? Have you seen those before?</div> </div> </div> </div>The video in #248 is named Pili (\u9739\u9742 / \u9739\u96f3\u5e03\u888b\u620f), a Taiwanese puppet show, it appeared in Taiwan around 1980 or so and is very popular for some reasons.<br /> <br /> The first two video from #267 are a collection of many wuxia TV series being put together, they do put the series's names in the video. The third is House of Flying Dagger, the fourth is the Return of the Condor Hero (the 2006 version) and some wuxia series that I don't know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T22:11:11-08:00","id":418417,"title":"","content":"Are those kung fu puppet shows still being made?<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with Condor Hero: I first encountered it as a comic book adaptation by Comics One called <a href=\"https://d1466nnw0ex81e.cloudfront.net/n_iv/600/967169.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">The Legendary Couple.</a> Later, I managed to get a boxset of the 2006 series. Also started the anime series, but never actually finished it...I was only half-watching a wuxia movie on the El Rey network when I started noticing some familiar names and plot details, and realized that it was yet another adaptation, called The Brave Archer trilogy (I DVR'd them but have yet to find time to watch them). <br /> <br /> Maybe one day I'll actually read the novels!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've heard that Condor Hero is remade every few years or so. Which adaptation do you like the most?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:00:14-08:00","id":418496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/61406-exalted-media?p=418388#post418388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The video in #248 is named Pili (\u9739\u9742 / \u9739\u96f3\u5e03\u888b\u620f), a Taiwanese puppet show, it appeared in Taiwan around 1980 or so and is very popular for some reasons.<br /> <br /> The first two video from #267 are a collection of many wuxia TV series being put together, they do put the series's names in the video. The third is House of Flying Dagger, the fourth is the Return of the Condor Hero (the 2006 version) and some wuxia series that I don't know of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Don't recognize any ones beyond the ones mentioned, but that is DEFINITELY Dissenting Monk* in the last video.<br /> <br /> *Seriously, pretty much every Shaolin movie I've seen, they cast the same guy to be the monk who takes issue with the main characters, but I can never remember his name for the life of me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:26:44-08:00","id":419798,"title":"","content":"Zekka, from Battle Angel Alita: Last Order, explains to us the appeal of being a Dusk Caste Abyssal:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i28.mangareader.net/battle-angel-alita-last-order/60/battle-angel-alita-last-order-982129.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i16.mangareader.net/battle-angel-alita-last-order/60/battle-angel-alita-last-order-982130.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:49:05-08:00","id":422606,"title":"","content":"Been watching a new anime series that's coming out called Seiken Tsukai no World Break. Let me start off by saying, it's not all that good, though it did remind me quite a bit of Exalted. <br /> <br /> The premise of the series was fairly interesting. It takes place in a modern world setting, where the world has been under siege by massive behemoth-like monsters that appear and begin smashing cities. Meanwhile, people are being born with the souls of ancient heroes from the past - great warriors or powerful mages. These people retain the memories from their past lives, so they know ancient magical spells or combat techniques that have been long forgotten. The world has academies set up to train these reborn heroes, and then uses those heroes to protect the world from those behemoth-like monsters. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the main character's soul was a hero in not just one, but two of it's previous incarnations (in one he was an incredibly powerful knight-warrior and in the other he was a edgy evil wizard). Unfortunately, the series falls into too many standard anime cliches, and it hasn't really done much with the past-incarnations beyond using them as an excuse to get the two main heroines to fall in love with the MC (each one lived with the MC in one of his past lives and was in love with him back then), or using his past experiences as a method of giving him a super-powerup (as he remembers the ultra powerful techniques he used to know). <br /> <br /> The first four episodes though weren't overly terrible, and might be worth checking out. I did like the magic system - it involves them writing runes of power into mid-air and looked fairly neat, and you tend not to see the idea of reincarnation used like that in most mass media, so it stood out for that at least, even if it isn't handling the idea particularly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:02:58-08:00","id":422620,"title":"","content":"The first few minutes of Seiken Tsukai no World Break gave me such hope for the series.<br /> <br /> It starts out with the main character (a Solar analogue) fighting an extremely powerful dragon. Though the hero flies through the air and strikes with sword and spell, he cannot match the beast alone.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, <i>Terrestrial Exalted</i>, dozens of them! &quot;We are The Saviors!&quot; And they throw up a massive energy shield that protects the Solar from being struck by the dragon's return fire.<br /> <br /> The Solar immediately takes this reprieve to begin writing runes into the air for a Celestial/Solar Circle Spell strong enough to defeat the dragon. While he's doing that, all of the Terrestrials are either maintaining the shield or wolf-packing the Dragon, combining their efforts and powers to inflict damage the Solar apparently couldn't manage alone.<br /> <br /> Even when the spotlight returns to the hero as he finishes the spell and moves in for the kill, he actually THANKS them all for making it possible. I can't remember the last time that a main character Solar-type hero seriously respected and appreciated the effort of his Terrestrial supporting cast.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then the flash-forward ends, and show almost immediately slumps into tired harem antics. Two girls near-immediately fall all over the hero -- which would be fine by itself, since they were apparently both his lovers in one or the other of his two previous lives.<br /> <br /> Except one of them was his sister in a past life. At first I thought the anime was going to maintain its level of quality and fake me out by actually having a totally platonic &quot;reborn siblings&quot; relationship instead of the romantic one that was hinted at... but no, she's a total brother-lover who's excited that they're not related this time. BLARGH. And it doesn't help that she's really annoying.<br /> <br /> The other girl is just... tastelessly shameless. And where the first girl is annoying, this one is just boring. Neither girl gets enough time to be properly introduced and fleshed out before they become arm-candy shoved into your face.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ridiculously big-breasted principal telling the hero how special he is after he gets kissed awake by an EXTREMELY under-aged girl was just the final nail in the coffin.<br /> <br /> <br /> But man, for those glorious first five minutes, and the show that could have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T23:30:10-08:00","id":422639,"title":"","content":"Noted. And speaking of silly shows with incredibly badass opening scenes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g458RvdtBbo\" data-code=\"g458RvdtBbo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/g458RvdtBbo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank